    "created_at": "2020-05-19T15:20:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-19T15:20:59Z",
    "body": "One potential issue I noticed is that this places the browsing contexts into new BCGs, but this does not modify anything in the WindowProxy/Location object definitions (e.g. [perform a security check](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#integration-with-idl)).\r\n\r\nIn the openee -> opener direction, this is fine, because `window.opener` is null, so there is no way to access the opener `WindowProxy`.\r\n\r\nIn the opener -> openee direction, I am less sure. I think because we discard the opened browsing context, we end up with `openee.closed === true`. But what is the intention if we do `openee.document`?\r\n\r\nMaybe this is https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5350, which we've decided to defer?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
