    "created_at": "2020-06-12T12:28:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-12T12:28:19Z",
    "body": "I think this is wrong for navigating to a response (initial fetching of `<object data>` also goes through this) and I'm not entirely sure to what extent we should address it here versus leaving it as it doesn't impact COOP I think. I wonder if we can assert that it doesn't happen in a top-level browsing context, but we should probably tackle that separately.\r\n\r\nFor `javascript:` URLs we have various open issues, but I think the important conclusion we reached was that they could not impact the existing policy in any way. So they are effectively a no-op as far as COOP goes.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
